 a  lot of segregation that existed and  separation so from a contextual  standpoint what I believe my father was  saying is that America in its founding  documentation documents essentially  talked about the dignity and Worth and  freedom of all human beings so it was  not just written as a document for one  ethnic group it was written for everyone  and and also everyone had the ability to  achieve his or her own dream of if he or  she was treated with dignity and respect  I think the speech is absolutely  relevant today as we are going through a  lot of division within our nation and  really divisions I should say in our  worlds we are attempting to be  segregated and separated and dad told us  how to disagree without being  disagreeable and I think that's  something we need to learn not just in  the political discourse but in the whole  discourse of our nation we will not be  able to achieve greatness if we are at  each other's necks as we are today
 

